Phase 1 — Read and annotate

The labels below replace handwritten annotations: DATA marks personal-data evidence, SPECIAL marks possible Article 9/10 data, TRANSFER marks an international-transfer question, PURPOSE marks a purpose-limitation issue, and CLARIFY marks missing evidence.

Evidence from the brief and architecture

Annotation

Audit significance

Intake contains organisation name, website, country, research period, and a free-text current_challenge.

DATA / CLARIFY

Organisation data is not automatically personal data, but the free-text field can contain employee, client, beneficiary, or contact information.

The live workflow researches public web sources and produces source-linked evidence, findings, inferences, hypotheses, and unknowns.

DATA / SPECIAL / PURPOSE

Public availability does not remove GDPR protection. The workflow may collect or infer information about identifiable staff, founders, donors, partners, or beneficiaries, including sensitive traits.

Outputs include source URLs, publishers, claims, confidence values, findings, and validation questions.

DATA / SPECIAL

These become personal data when linked or linkable to a person. Inferences may be sensitive even when the source did not state them explicitly.

Consultants select questions and next steps, add notes, and make the Draft/Ready decision.

DATA / PURPOSE

Notes can include personal data. Human review reduces automated-decision risk but does not itself create a lawful basis.

Browser state and notes are session-only and reset on reload; uploaded files are not sent in the current MVP.

DATA

This is a minimisation safeguard. It does not establish the retention period for n8n executions, API vendors, server logs, or backups.

The browser calls an n8n webhook; public research and transformation occur upstream.

TRANSFER / CLARIFY

Provider identities, processing locations, subprocessors, and transfer mechanisms are not documented in the reviewed evidence.

A direct browser-to-workflow connection cannot protect a secret; an authenticated gateway, restricted CORS, rate limits, redacted logs, restricted execution access, and deletion/retention rules are still required for production.

DATA / CLARIFY

The builders have identified material Article 25 and 32 production gaps.

The workflow distinguishes facts, inferences, hypotheses, and unknowns and requires validation of non-observed findings.

PURPOSE

Useful accuracy and fairness safeguard, but it does not prevent incompatible reuse, model training, or person-level profiling unless those uses are contractually and technically prohibited.

